nvidia-kmod-legacy-580xx (580.196.07-1+sparky1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * NVIDIA's 580 driver, the last branch for Maxwell, Pascal and Volta cards,
    for the edition's kernels (ORDER 354). The upstream tarball is the DKMS
    tree /usr/src/nvidia-580.196.07 of NVIDIA's nvidia-kernel-dkms
    580.196.07-1 from NVIDIA's CUDA repository for Debian 12, unmodified. It
    builds on Linux 7.3.0 and 7.3.1 (stereo3d13 base and real-time,
    stereo3d14 base, x86-64-v3 and real-time) with no patch.
  * Two binary packages: nvidia-legacy-580xx-kernel-dkms, which provides
    nvidia-kernel-dkms at NVIDIA's exact version, and
    sparky-stereo-nvidia-legacy-580xx-driver-lock, the APT lock generated
    from the same version. NVIDIA publishes the 580 user space for Debian only
    in its repository for Debian 12, which Debian 14's APT refuses (its key's
    binding signature is SHA-1), so the lock names no source for it.
  * NVIDIA's own package depends on firmware-nvidia-gsp at its version; this
    one does not: GSP firmware runs only on Turing cards and newer, which the
    edition's open modules drive, and NVIDIA publishes the 580 copy only in
    that Debian 12 repository.
  * Depends on gcc: NVIDIA's build calls cc, and the edition's kernel headers
    bring only gcc-16-for-host (x86_64-linux-gnu-gcc-16).

 -- Daniel Ramos (Capitain Jack) <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 17:30:00 -0300
